-- an interaction whose kernel is a product is half the square of a one-particle operator, less half its self term:
-- ½ G² = V + ½ self, for every g. (The repulsion is a positive sum of such kernels: the Gaussian transform of 1/r.)
fs-square : fa-eq AlP al-add al-mul al-q al-isz (fa-scal AlP al-mul (al-q (fn-q 1 2)) (fa-mul AlP al-add al-mul al-q fs-G fs-G)) (fa-add AlP al-add fs-V (fa-scal AlP al-mul (al-q (fn-q 1 2)) fs-self)) ≡ true
fs-square = λ i → true
